    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "I apologize if this question has already been answered or explained elsewhere that I could not find.\r\n\r\nIn most cases, I think `search_method = 'cover_or_next'` is the best. However, when working with `ai.gen_spec.treesitter()` textobjects, I find that the \"or_next\" part gets annoying; that is, I want these specific textobjects to only match when my cursor is within their bounds (which I believe `search_method = 'cover'` does), for example to prevent jumping 30 line down when I do a cif. Is there a way of specifying `search_method` for different textobjects? (I don't see anything obvious [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.ai/blob/45587078f323eaf41b9f701bbc04f8d1ab008979/lua/mini/ai.lua#L959)...)\r\n\r\nPS. I absolutely love what you're doing with mini.nvim, thanks for the awesome work <3",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I apologize if this question has already been answered or explained elsewhere that I could not find.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In most cases, I think <code class=\"notranslate\">search_method = 'cover_or_next'</code> is the best. However, when working with <code class=\"notranslate\">ai.gen_spec.treesitter()</code> textobjects, I find that the \"or_next\" part gets annoying; that is, I want these specific textobjects to only match when my cursor is within their bounds (which I believe <code class=\"notranslate\">search_method = 'cover'</code> does), for example to prevent jumping 30 line down when I do a cif. Is there a way of specifying <code class=\"notranslate\">search_method</code> for different textobjects? (I don't see anything obvious <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.ai/blob/45587078f323eaf41b9f701bbc04f8d1ab008979/lua/mini/ai.lua#L959\">here</a>...)</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">PS. I absolutely love what you're doing with mini.nvim, thanks for the awesome work &lt;3</p>",
    "bodyText": "I apologize if this question has already been answered or explained elsewhere that I could not find.\nIn most cases, I think search_method = 'cover_or_next' is the best. However, when working with ai.gen_spec.treesitter() textobjects, I find that the \"or_next\" part gets annoying; that is, I want these specific textobjects to only match when my cursor is within their bounds (which I believe search_method = 'cover' does), for example to prevent jumping 30 line down when I do a cif. Is there a way of specifying search_method for different textobjects? (I don't see anything obvious here...)\nPS. I absolutely love what you're doing with mini.nvim, thanks for the awesome work <3",
