                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Yes, this is one way of doing this.\r\n\r\nAnother approach is to create custom mappings for `a(` and `i(` in Visual and Operator-pending modes. With something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal map_cover_parens = function(mode, ai_type, id)\r\n  local opts = { search_method = 'cover', operator_pending = mode == 'o' }\r\n  local rhs = function()\r\n    opts.n_times = vim.v.count1\r\n    MiniAi.select_textobject(ai_type, id, opts)\r\n  end\r\n  local desc = (ai_type == 'a' and 'Around' or 'Inside') .. ' covering ' .. vim.inspect(id)\r\n  vim.keymap.set(mode, ai_type .. id, rhs, { desc = desc })\r\nend\r\n\r\nmap_cover_parens('x', 'a', '(')\r\nmap_cover_parens('x', 'i', '(')\r\nmap_cover_parens('o', 'a', '(')\r\nmap_cover_parens('o', 'i', '(')\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is more verbose, but should be less cryptic.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, I don't see a better way of doing this. Maybe `find_textobject()` might be extended to accept specification directly as `id` argument.\r\n\r\nBut nevertheless, the main suggestion still stands: use `'cover'` method as the main one and explicitly use `an` / `al` / `in` / `il` variants if you want next/previous textobject.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, this is one way of doing this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Another approach is to create custom mappings for <code class=\"notranslate\">a(</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">i(</code> in Visual and Operator-pending modes. With something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local map_cover_parens = function(mode, ai_type, id)\n  local opts = { search_method = 'cover', operator_pending = mode == 'o' }\n  local rhs = function()\n    opts.n_times = vim.v.count1\n    MiniAi.select_textobject(ai_type, id, opts)\n  end\n  local desc = (ai_type == 'a' and 'Around' or 'Inside') .. ' covering ' .. vim.inspect(id)\n  vim.keymap.set(mode, ai_type .. id, rhs, { desc = desc })\nend\n\nmap_cover_parens('x', 'a', '(')\nmap_cover_parens('x', 'i', '(')\nmap_cover_parens('o', 'a', '(')\nmap_cover_parens('o', 'i', '(')\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">map_cover_parens</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">ai_type</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">id</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">opts</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">search_method</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>cover<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">operator_pending</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>o<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>}\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">rhs</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">opts</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">n_times</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">v</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">count1</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniAi</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">select_textobject</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">ai_type</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">id</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">opts</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> (<span class=\"pl-smi\">ai_type</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>a<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Around<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Inside<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span> covering <span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">inspect</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">id</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">ai_type</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">id</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">rhs</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> })\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">map_cover_parens</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>x<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>a<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>(<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">map_cover_parens</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>x<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>i<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>(<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">map_cover_parens</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>o<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>a<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>(<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">map_cover_parens</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>o<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>i<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>(<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is more verbose, but should be less cryptic.</p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Unfortunately, I don't see a better way of doing this. Maybe <code class=\"notranslate\">find_textobject()</code> might be extended to accept specification directly as <code class=\"notranslate\">id</code> argument.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But nevertheless, the main suggestion still stands: use <code class=\"notranslate\">'cover'</code> method as the main one and explicitly use <code class=\"notranslate\">an</code> / <code class=\"notranslate\">al</code> / <code class=\"notranslate\">in</code> / <code class=\"notranslate\">il</code> variants if you want next/previous textobject.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Yes, this is one way of doing this.\nAnother approach is to create custom mappings for a( and i( in Visual and Operator-pending modes. With something like this:\nlocal map_cover_parens = function(mode, ai_type, id)\n  local opts = { search_method = 'cover', operator_pending = mode == 'o' }\n  local rhs = function()\n    opts.n_times = vim.v.count1\n    MiniAi.select_textobject(ai_type, id, opts)\n  end\n  local desc = (ai_type == 'a' and 'Around' or 'Inside') .. ' covering ' .. vim.inspect(id)\n  vim.keymap.set(mode, ai_type .. id, rhs, { desc = desc })\nend\n\nmap_cover_parens('x', 'a', '(')\nmap_cover_parens('x', 'i', '(')\nmap_cover_parens('o', 'a', '(')\nmap_cover_parens('o', 'i', '(')\nThis is more verbose, but should be less cryptic.\n\nUnfortunately, I don't see a better way of doing this. Maybe find_textobject() might be extended to accept specification directly as id argument.\nBut nevertheless, the main suggestion still stands: use 'cover' method as the main one and explicitly use an / al / in / il variants if you want next/previous textobject.",
